{
	title: 'Compact and retry when the prompt is too long',
	spec: 'When a provider refuses a round because the prompt is too long (Anthropic "prompt is too long", OpenAI context_length_exceeded, or a 400/413 whose message says so), that is no temporary failure to retry forever: the host compacts (task bc) and retries the round once, telling the user with a notice ("the provider said the prompt is too long: compacted, trying again"); if the compacted request is refused again, the turn fails with the provider message. The compact goes only between rounds, after results are recorded, never between a tool call and its result. The current turn starts at its initiating prompt, even when a paused (or failed) turn is continued with Enter after a turn_end record; its original prompt and every later prompt delivered into that same turn stay after the boundary verbatim, including images (the compact record\'s `keep`); only the context before them is summarized, although the boundary is written after the prompt in append-only history. Its main use: switching mid-session to a model with a smaller window. There is no compaction at a usage threshold: it was built and dropped, because with 1M-token windows and sessions that stay under about 250k tokens it never fired, and early compaction trades an exact context for a lossy summary mid-task; /compact is the user\'s tool for that. Tests: a too-long error compacts and retries once, then fails; the provider wordings are recognized and others are not; the retried request keeps the new prompt and its image outside the summary, also after a restart; a paused turn resumed with Enter keeps its original prompt; several prompts spanning pauses all remain.',
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		'compact.retry (src/host/compact.ts) runs in turns.runTurn before the failure/backoff branch, at most once per turn, and deletes the error failure so a too-long refusal is never retried as temporary. The notice is a plain output record (slash.output).',
		'Append-only boundaries can reference original prompt record numbers (compact.keep); provider replay places them after the summary with original image blocks, while summary excludes those records. No duplicate display prompt is written. A kept prompt record that also holds tool results replays only its text and images: its results have no call after the boundary and are dropped.',
		'The last turn_end is not a reliable current-turn boundary: pause and error ends are durable but a following continue resumes the same original prompt. Walk past ends only when their following segment contains continue; stop at a completed end or an uncontinued end.'
	],
	needs: [
		'bc'
	]
}
